  ESI Assistive Backpack - item tracking sketch (RFID + DFPlayer + LCD + RGB)
  This program helps users check that they have packed the correct items for a 
  selected activity. Intended for dementia patients.

  Written by Callum Storrar
  Utilises library by Oliver Mckinlay
  Created: 17/9/26
  Last Edited: 18/10/26

  The LCD circuit:
 * LCD RS pin to digital pin 22
 * LCD Enable pin to digital pin 23
 * LCD D4 pin to digital pin 24
 * LCD D5 pin to digital pin 25
 * LCD D6 pin to digital pin 26
 * LCD D7 pin to digital pin 27
 * LCD R/W pin to ground
 * wiper to LCD VO pin to resistance to ground

  The RGB circuit:
 * Red Pin (next to cathode) to 220ohm to digital pin 4
 * Cathode Pin to ground
 * Green Pin to 220ohm to digital pin 3
 * Blue Pin to 220ohm to digital pin 2

  The RFID circuit (4x MFRC522, Mega hardware SPI):
 * Reader 1 SDA/SS to digital pin 37
 * Reader 2 SDA/SS to digital pin 39
 * Reader 3 SDA/SS to digital pin 41
 * Reader 4 SDA/SS to digital pin 43
 * Reader 1 RST to digital pin 36
 * Reader 2 RST to digital pin 38
 * Reader 3 RST to digital pin 40
 * Reader 4 RST to digital pin 42
 * All readers SCK to pin 52 (shared)
 * All readers MOSI to pin 51 (shared)
 * All readers MISO to pin 50 (shared)
 * All readers 3.3V to 3.3V (NOT 5V) and GND to ground

  DFPlayer Mini (SoftwareSerial):
 * DFPlayer TX to digital pin 13
 * DFPlayer RX to digital pin 12 through a 1k resistor
 * VCC to 5V, GND to ground

 created 17 Sept 2026
 by Callum Storrar
*/

